      "answer": "The current ingress-class policy is `policy/ingress-class/v3.yaml`, and it now proposes `envoy-gateway` in [PR #158](https://github.com/dshnayder-org/infra/pull/158) against `git-access-ab/r200`. Branch: `platform-agent/ingress-class-envoy-gateway-r200`, commit `b52f745`, one file, `+1 -1`.\n\n## Which file is current, and why\n\n`policy/ingress-class/` holds three versions. `v3.yaml` is the only one marked current — verbatim, both in the YAML and in the header comment:\n\n- `v3.yaml` — `  status: current` and `# version: v3   effective: 2026-04-19   status: current`; `  effectiveFrom: 2026-04-19` is the latest of the three.\n- `v1.yaml` — `  status: superseded`, header `# version: v1   effective: 2024-03-11   status: superseded by v2`, `  setting: nginx`. **Untouched.**\n- `v2.yaml` — `  status: superseded`, header `# version: v2   effective: 2025-06-02   status: superseded by v3`, `  setting: gce-ingress`. **Untouched.**\n\nThere is no index or README pointing at a live doc; the `status:` field plus the `superseded by vN` header chain is the marker. The other five policies in `policy/` (`backup-schedule`, `key-rotation`, `log-retention`, `node-image`, `psa-mode`) use the identical v1/v2/v3 + `status:` convention, which confirms the reading. The value replaced was `  setting: gateway-api`.\n\n## The diff\n\n```diff\n--- a/policy/ingress-class/v3.yaml\n+++ b/policy/ingress-class/v3.yaml\n@@ -10,4 +10,4 @@ metadata:\n spec:\n   effectiveFrom: 2026-04-19\n   status: current\n-  setting: gateway-api\n+  setting: envoy-gateway\n```\n\n`effectiveFrom`, `status`, `metadata.name` and the header comment are unchanged — tell me if the effective date should move forward with the rollout.\n\n## One thing I fixed on the way\n\n`submit-suggestion`'s content mode never passed a base branch to the credential broker, so it cut from and targeted the repo's default branch (`main`) and ignored both `GITOPS_BASE_BRANCH` and any card-specified base — the first `prepare` here came back `\"base\": \"main\"`. I added a `--base` flag honoured by both modes and updated the skill doc. Worth knowing: any earlier PR from this path that was meant for a non-default base likely landed on `main`.",
