      "answer": "`scripts/rotate-keys.sh` is executable, so `scripts/drain-pool.sh` was committed executable to match: both are `100755` on the branch. [PR #159](https://github.com/dshnayder-org/infra/pull/159) is open against `git-access-ab/r200`.\n\n## Modes\n\n| File | Mode |\n| --- | --- |\n| `scripts/rotate-keys.sh` | `100755` |\n| `scripts/drain-pool.sh` | `100755` |\n\n`scripts/rotate-keys.sh` reads `100755` (executable) on `git-access-ab/r200`, read from the branch's git tree, not inferred. `scripts/drain-pool.sh` was committed at `100755` and verified as `100755` on the pushed branch after the fact. The file's own comment says it must stay executable — a workflow runs it directly rather than through `bash`.\n\n## The script\n\nMirrors `rotate-keys.sh` exactly: `#!/usr/bin/env bash`, `set -euo pipefail`, and the same `${1:?cluster required}` argument check. Takes a cluster name and prints a drain plan — cordon, evict respecting PodDisruptionBudgets, wait, uncordon on abort. It mutates nothing; every line is an `echo`. Verified by running it: prints the plan for a named cluster, exits `1` with `cluster required` when given no argument.\n\n## What the repo does not contain\n\n- **No `.github/workflows/`** — `rotate-keys.sh`'s comment references `.github/workflows/rotate.yml`, but no `.github` tree exists on this branch, so nothing here invokes either script. The executable bit still matters for whatever runs it elsewhere.\n- **No existing `drain-pool.sh`** — `scripts/` held only `rotate-keys.sh`.\n- **No linter or test config** covering `scripts/`. `.gitattributes` has one rule, for `docs/generated/*.txt`, which does not touch this file. `shellcheck` is not installed here, so the script was checked with `bash -n` and by running it.\n\n## Tooling gaps found and fixed\n\nThe shipped `submit-suggestion` helper could not do this task; it would have silently produced a wrong PR. Both gaps are patched in `/opt/data/skills/submit-suggestion/scripts/submit_suggestion.py` and documented in the skill:\n\n- **Base branch ignored** — content-mode `prepare` always opened on the repo default, so this PR would have targeted `main`, not `git-access-ab/r200`, with a diff against the wrong tree. Added `--base`.\n- **Mode always `100644`** — no way to commit an executable file, so `drain-pool.sh` would have landed non-executable while the diff looked correct. Added `--mode <path>=100755`, which refuses a path not in the change set rather than ignoring it.",
